# objective_c 9.6.2: deterministic private debug paths

This is a minimal local copy of the resolved objective_c 9.6.2 package. Runtime
lib/ and native src/ files are unchanged from upstream. LICENSE, README.md,
CHANGELOG.md and pubspec.yaml are retained. The published package has no AUTHORS
file; its original copyright and license notices remain intact.

Only hook/build.dart is patched. The hook invokes clang directly and ignores
CFLAGS/Xcode OTHER_CFLAGS, so this path override applies the flags at the owning
compile boundary instead of modifying the shared package cache or global tools.

The hook retains -gline-tables-only and all existing target/link flags. It adds
-ffile-prefix-map and -fdebug-prefix-map for the package parent, current working
directory, build output and finally the specific package root. Clang's last
matching prefix wins; the last mapping is /packages/objective_c. An explicit
-fdebug-compilation-dir uses that same portable directory. Metadata paths change;
function symbols, source-relative filenames and line tables remain available.

Source provenance and SHA-256 hashes are registered in
scripts/maintenance/path_override_upstream_hashes.json, including the original
and patched hook hashes. The package version and runtime/native sources are not
upgraded. No post-link editing or UUID rewriting is performed. Each rebuild must
produce matching framework/dSYM UUIDs through the existing iOS archive checker.

Validation after resolving this override:
- Run the existing path-override upstream-hash check.
- Analyze hook/build.dart with the project SDK.
- Rebuild native assets and the iOS candidate; do not reuse the old objective_c
  framework/dSYM cache. Keep uploadSymbols enabled.
- Check both Runner.app and the exported IPA with check_private_content.py.
  The export check includes Symbols/*.symbols, not only the signed payload.
